## std.time — Duration + Timer primitives.
##
## From docs/spec.md §6.2 + §6.4.4: timers live in std.time, exposed
## as future-returning async-fun bodies that hand control to the
## event loop. The current parser doesn't accept `async fun`'s full
## surface (per docs/features.md), so the stub uses sync free functions
## whose names mirror the eventual API (`Timer_after`, etc.) — the
## async layer swaps in beneath these names without breaking call sites.
##
## Stub: sync surface only. Real impl lands via the event loop's
## built-in timer wheel in zig std.event.

pub struct Duration {
    nanos: i64,
}

pub fun Duration_from_millis(ms: i64) -> Duration {
    return Duration { nanos: ms };
}

pub struct Timer {
    _opaque: i32,
}

pub fun Timer_after(d: Duration) -> bool {
    return false;
}
